        "text": "Level, momentum, one-off, and policy mechanisms are separated as follows: the level remains near 4%; momentum eased by 0.6 percentage point from March to May; volatile fuel, travel, and food can move individual months; and electricity-rebate exhaustion keeps Housing inflation elevated. These effects support a central value near 4.0% without extrapolating March's spike."
